                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Proposals to allow college students to sleep in their cars is a symptom of a housing crisis that is hurting students and everyday Californians. \n\nThis is a consequence of policy failures coming from a liberal agenda that refuses to allow for the building of more housing, further worsening California\u2019s affordability crisis. \n\nIn dealing with a growing housing and homelessness emergency, California doesn\u2019t need more parking lots, we need real solutions that cut red tape and end frivolous litigation so we can unleash housing development and build real roofs with real beds. \n\nhttps://t.co/opOUbHgXvz",
